 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? You don't need to speak to help. Listening is the biggest thing, so any language you can understand is helpful. I' fairly sure about it. Would you like me to check and I say it with confidence? Then ask her teacher for a plan. They usually send homework and can tell you which level she's at. Some might, at first. But every time she says something, like her name or what she's hungry for, build it into a conversation. Try matching phrases she says in French with English. Once she knows the words, she'll start mixing them herself.",
